From 2924ddc97231ebfdae373b5c7077ac222b09de18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:30:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: a sharded kept state's pages stay in one part; the
 shared store's disk glue

One-part invariant for kept paths under TF_GLM_KV_SHARD (a skipped resume seats at its prefix's part; a cross-part keep replaces or is refused, kv_shard_keeps_refused_total). Disk glue found on two DGX Sparks: a share step makes every rank follow rank 0's share_pages for the identity probe, the store's family carries GLM's disk image, the host's idle turns drive the paged store's writer, and a write-behind carries the state's pages from its first token.
